{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"98f03af7-d03a-4ffb-a629-4b6b3aec77b6","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\n  \"doc_id\": \"keepass\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-001\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"KeePass must be downloaded and installed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Passive phrasing omits the actor responsible for downloading and installing KeePass, as well as the download source, target platform/OS, version, and what functionality this preconditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-002\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Master Password has no limits in length. A whole sentence can be used with more than 100 characters.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'No limits in length' is ambiguous as to whether zero-length (empty) passwords are allowed and is untestable as an unbounded maximum; 'A whole sentence can be used' is illustrative rather than a precise constraint.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-002\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Master Password has no limits in length.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify minimum password length (e.g., non-empty), allowed character set or encoding, or any practical upper bound.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflates a 'Folder' with a '.kdb' file, states that 'the database can read' rather than the application, and leaves unclear whether 'name' is a placeholder or literal and whether the extension is case-sensitive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system behavior or error handling if an unsupported file type or a folder is selected, nor the actor or operation (open, save, import) to which this applies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Databases must have different names or else the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains typos ('previews', 'replace') and ambiguous referents: it is unclear what 'the previews one' and 'if selected' refer to (e.g., choosing the same name vs. confirming an overwrite prompt), and 'different names' does not clarify scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Databases must have different names or else the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify the scope of name uniqueness (same directory vs. system-wide), case sensitivity, or whether the user is warned and asked for confirmation before overwriting an existing database.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-005\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There must be entries in the database in order for them to be printed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system behavior when a user attempts to print an empty database (e.g., disable printing or display an error message), nor the actor or scope of which entries are printed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word must be shown.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Related to' is vague (substring vs. exact match, case sensitivity), 'the word' lacks a defined referent, and 'All data' is inconsistent with the example's 'both entries must be shown' regarding whether sensitive fields like passwords are shown.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word must be shown.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens when no entries match the search term or when the search input is empty, nor which entry fields are searched.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-007\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the new group/subgroup to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system behavior if a user omits the name or enters a blank name, nor validation constraints on valid group/subgroup names (length, allowed characters, uniqueness) or the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-008\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A subgroup cannot be created when no group is selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify how the system enforces this restriction or responds when a user attempts to create a subgroup with no group selected (e.g., disabling the option or displaying an error message).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-009\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the group/subgroup to be renamed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system behavior if the user submits an empty or missing name when renaming a group/subgroup, nor constraints on valid names (length, characters, uniqueness).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In order to find something in a group a word must be placed in the find field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Something' does not specify which items or entry fields are searched, and 'a word' is ambiguous as to whether multi-word phrases, substrings, or special characters are permitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In order to find something in a group a word must be placed in the find field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens if the find field is empty when search is triggered or if no matches are found, nor what triggers the search or how results are displayed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"syntactic\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Awkward phrasing implies an entry must belong to a group before it exists; it is ambiguous whether a group must be pre-selected before invoking creation or can be chosen during entry creation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system behavior when no group is selected or exists during an attempt to create an entry (e.g., error message, disabled UI option, or default group assignment).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-012\",\n      