ts to view or modify with no entry selected (or with multiple entries selected), nor the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-015\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is changed the repeat password field must be Changed and be identical with password field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system error handling if the repeat password field is not updated or does not match the modified password field, nor which context/dialog this applies to.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is changed the repeat password field must be Changed and be identical with password field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-012\",\n        \"KP-013\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Duplicates KP-013's unconditional requirement that the password and repeat password fields must be identical, and overlaps KP-012's requirement to complete the repeat password field when the password field is filled.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-016\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must be selected before it is duplicated\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify system behavior when duplication is attempted with no entry (or multiple entries) selected, nor how the duplicated entry's attributes (e.g., title, group) are populated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-017\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An internet connection and a browser are required in order to download new language translations For the following features, use cases are not included\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The trailing note 'For the following features, use cases are not included' is merged without punctuation and has an unbounded referent ('the following features'); 'a browser' is also unspecified regarding supported browsers or versions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-017\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An internet connection and a browser are required in order to download new language translations For the following features, use cases are not included\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Explicitly notes omitted use-case specifications for subsequent features and omits the download source, supported browsers, installation procedure, and error handling when offline or no browser is available.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-018\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The prefix “Auto-Type:” is required in front of each sequence\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Sequence' is never defined in the SRS (its syntax, purpose, and valid tokens are unstated), and it is unclear whether the 'Auto-Type:' prefix is case-sensitive or whitespace-sensitive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-018\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The prefix “Auto-Type:” is required in front of each sequence\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify where sequences are entered (only implied later in KP-020 as a note field) or what the system does if the 'Auto-Type:' prefix is omitted or malformed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-019\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Sequence’s length must not be more than a line (59 characters)\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Sequence' is undefined, 'a line (59 characters)' conflates a visual line with a fixed character count, and it is unclear whether the 59-character limit includes the 'Auto-Type:' prefix.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-019\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Sequence’s length must not be more than a line (59 characters)\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens if a sequence exceeds 59 characters (e.g., rejected with an error, truncated, or ignored).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-020\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"If two auto-types are referred in one note field, only the first is used\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'Referred' is vague (unclear whether it means defined with 'Auto-Type:', listed, or invoked), and specifying 'two auto-types' leaves unclear whether the same rule applies to three or more.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-020\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"If two auto-types are referred in one note field, only the first is used\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify behavior when more than two auto-types appear in a single note field, nor whether the user is warned that additional auto-types are ignored.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-020\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"two auto-types\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-018\",\n        \"KP-019\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Refers to the feature as 'auto-types' rather than 'sequence' with the 'Auto-Type:' prefix as termed in KP-018 and KP-019.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-021\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Only one database file is allowed in command line options\",\n      \"relate